      "text": "Let's solve the problem step by step.\n\nGiven the point \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\), we can express \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(t\\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\nWe need to eliminate the parameter \\(t\\) to find the relationship between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\). From the expressions for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), we can solve for \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\) and then substitute it into the expression for \\(y\\):\n\\[ x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\implies \\frac{1}{t} = x - 1 \\implies t = \\frac{1}{x - 1} \\]\n\\[ y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} = 1 - (x - 1) = 2 - x \\]\n\nSo we have the relationship:\n\\[ y = 2 - x \\]\n\nThis is the equation of a line. Therefore, the plotted points lie on a line.\n\nThe correct option is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
