      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the type of curve on which all the plotted points \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie, we start by expressing \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(t\\):\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\nWe can eliminate \\(t\\) by expressing \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\). From the equation for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[ x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\implies \\frac{1}{t} = x - 1 \\implies t = \\frac{1}{x-1} \\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(t = \\frac{1}{x-1}\\) into the equation for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[ y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x-1}} = 1 - (x-1) = 2 - x \\]\n\nThis equation shows that \\(y\\) is a linear function of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[ y = 2 - x \\]\n\nThis is the equation of a line. Therefore, all the plotted points \\((x, y)\\) lie on a line.\n\nThe correct option is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
