      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine what kind of curve all the points \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie on, we need to eliminate the parameter \\(t\\) and express \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\).\n\nGiven the points: \n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\]\n\nFirst, we will express \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} \\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\(t\\) gives:\n\\[ x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\]\nRearranging the equation, we get:\n\\[ x - 1 = \\frac{1}{t} \\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\(t\\) gives:\n\\[ t(x - 1) = 1 \\]\n\\[ t = \\frac{1}{x - 1} \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(t = \\frac{1}{x - 1}\\) into the equation for \\(y\\):\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\]\nSubstituting \\(t = \\frac{1}{x - 1}\\) into this equation gives:\n\\[ y = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x - 1} - 1}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} \\]\nSimplify the numerator:\n\\[ y = \\frac{\\frac{1 - (x - 1)}{x - 1}}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} = \\frac{\\frac{1 - x + 1}{x - 1}}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} = \\frac{\\frac{2 - x}{x - 1}}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} = 2 - x \\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[ y = 2 - x \\]\n\nThis is the equation of a straight line. Therefore, the points \\((x, y)\\) lie on a line.\n\nThe correct option is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
